@startuml
title Physical database registration

participant "DBaaS Adapter" as Adapter
participant "DBaaS Aggregator" as Aggregator
database "DBaaS Registry" as Registry

Adapter -> Aggregator: register physical database\nPUT /api/v3/dbaas/{type}/physical_databases/{phydbid}\n(adapter address, credentials, supported roles, features)
note right of Aggregator
  A malformed adapter address is rejected
  with 400 Bad Request (CORE-DBAAS-4045).
end note

opt adapter reports status "run"
  Aggregator -> Adapter: check which physical database the adapter serves\nGET {adapterAddress}/api/v2/dbaas/adapter/{type}/physical_database
  Adapter --> Aggregator: served physical database id, or error
  alt adapter answers with a non-200 status
    Aggregator --> Adapter: 502 Bad Gateway (CORE-DBAAS-4017): adapter is unavailable
  else adapter answers with another physical database id
    Aggregator --> Adapter: 409 Conflict (CORE-DBAAS-4011): physical database id mismatch
  end
end

Aggregator -> Registry: find physical database by {phydbid}
Registry --> Aggregator: physical database registered with {phydbid}, if any
Aggregator -> Registry: find physical database by adapter address
Registry --> Aggregator: physical database registered with the adapter address, if any

alt physical database is registered
  alt adapter address or {phydbid} does not match the registration
    note right of Aggregator
      {phydbid} is registered with another adapter address,
      or adapter address is registered with another {phydbid}.
      Changing only the address protocol (HTTP or HTTPS) is allowed.
    end note
    Aggregator --> Adapter: 409 Conflict (CORE-DBAAS-4011): registration conflicts with an existing one

  else adapter address and {phydbid} match the registration
    alt supported roles changed, features.multiusers is true, some logical databases lack users for the new roles
      alt adapter status is "running" and API version is v2
        Aggregator -> Registry: save role migration plan,\nor resume the plan in progress
        Aggregator --> Adapter: 202 Accepted: portion of logical databases\nthat need users for new roles
        ref over Adapter, Registry: Additional roles migration
      else adapter status is not "running", or API version is not v2
        Aggregator --> Adapter: 400 Bad Request (no error code): adapter cannot run role migration
      end

    else supported roles are unchanged, features.multiusers is false,\nor no logical databases need users for the new roles
      opt registration data changed
        Aggregator -> Registry: update physical database\n(address, credentials, roles, features, labels)
      end
      Aggregator --> Adapter: 200 OK: registration is up to date
    end
  end

else physical database is not registered
  Aggregator -> Registry: save new physical database\n(the first one of its type becomes the default)
  Aggregator --> Adapter: 201 Created: physical database registered
end

legend bottom right
  Solid arrow: synchronous request. Dashed arrow: response.
  Every step runs inside the adapter's registration request.
  Registry write acknowledgements are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml

